__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# web/
# Unanchored, so it also catches the node_modules a tool leaves at the repo
# root when it is run from there rather than from web/ — vitest writes its
# cache into one, and sixteen of those files were committed once already.
node_modules/
web/dist/
.env

# The shore shadow: neither its source data nor its output belongs in git.
#
# The pyramid is 15,088 files and 55 MB — a binary artefact that would be in
# every clone of this repository forever, re-added wholesale on every
# re-render, and reviewable by nobody. It is a pure function of the renderer
# and of Natural Earth, both of which *are* in git, so the repository carries
# the recipe and each machine makes its own copy: a developer with
# `tools/build_shore_shadow.py`, a server with `georiva render_shore_shadow`.
# docs/shore-shadow.md has both.
#
# The Natural Earth zips are ignored for the older, simpler reason: nothing
# but a re-render reads them, and a re-render can fetch them again.
web/public/shore-shadow/
.natural-earth/

# The built web bundle. It is committed exactly once per release, on the
# detached commit a tag points at, by .github/workflows/release.yml with
# `git add -f` — never on main, where a minified bundle would make every diff
# unreadable. Ignored here so that a local `npm run build`, which is how the
# bundle is checked before it ships, leaves a clean working tree.
src/georiva_forecast_viewer/static/forecast_viewer/
